# Line-ending policy for license texts.
#
# These files are redistributed verbatim inside the NSIS installer and alongside the
# portable artifacts. On checkouts where core.autocrlf=true (as on GitHub's windows
# runners) Git would otherwise rewrite LF to CRLF, so the *published* copies would no
# longer be byte-identical to the upstream texts -- e.g. RARLAB's license, whose
# clause 2 requires the verbatim text, or the SIL OFL text for the embedded fonts.
#
# Pinning eol=lf keeps source, repository and shipped copies identical on every platform.

LICENSE                  text eol=lf
licenses/**              text eol=lf
